# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  The Epicurean — environment
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  The interactive world map uses OpenFreeMap for tiles — NO key, NO
#  account, nothing to configure. It just works.
#
#  The only setup step is geocoding the 12,650 addresses into pin
#  coordinates, once:   npm run geocode
#
#  Geocoding works with ZERO signup (it falls back to OpenStreetMap
#  Nominatim). But Nominatim is capped at 1 request/second (~4 hours for
#  the full set) and is a little less accurate on messy addresses.
#
#  For a faster, more accurate run, get a FREE LocationIQ key (email
#  only, no credit card) at https://locationiq.com and paste it below.
#  The geocode script auto-detects it. The script is resumable, so you
#  can spread the run across days and stay within the free tier.
#
#  Copy this file to `.env` to use a key:
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# LOCATIONIQ_KEY=pk.your_locationiq_key_here
